license: MIT
date-released: 2026-04-23
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >
  This repository benchmarks seven forecasting approaches for day-ahead solar
  power prediction at a single 3.45 MW site over horizons D+1–D+3. Models are
  evaluated on two target formulations: the clear-sky performance index k and
  direct AC power. After a leakage audit and timestamp-alignment correction for
  LSTM predictions, XGBoost SOTA achieves the lowest nRMSE on both targets
  (indirect: 29.1%, direct: 12.1% at D+1). The indirect forecasting route
  (predict k, reconstruct power) outperforms direct AC-power forecasting by
  1.7–2.1 pp nRMSE at the operational scale for both model families. SHAP
  group analysis reveals that clear-sky geometry (15% of importance for indirect,
  <1% for direct) and rolling production statistics (52% vs 75%) swap hierarchy
  depending on target choice.
